// MeRegionalUnavailable is returned in place of MeRegional when the
// responding node is NOT the account's home jurisdiction. It names the
// jurisdiction that holds the regional view.
//
// `error` is the load-bearing discriminator — SPAs and SDKs pattern-
// match on `error === "foreign_jurisdiction"` to dispatch a
// "hosted elsewhere" state instead of treating an empty regional block
// as "no profile yet".
//
// It deliberately carries no console URL. There is no per-account profile
// page to link to (the user-facing console SPA was retired; a bare "/"
// redirects by role), and the console is an admin surface that a normal
// caller has no use for. Handing every caller a console origin advertised
// something both broken and internal. Admin-gating it instead was rejected:
// varying this block by the caller's role would let anyone probe their own
// platform-admin status from /me, which handleConsoleRoot is careful not to
// leak.
