// Names the jurisdiction holding the regional view, plus its core origin.
//
// The URL is the home jurisdiction's OIDC issuer (JurisdictionAuthHost),
// not its console (JurisdictionHost). It used to be the console, once with
// a "/#/profile" fragment naming a route that no longer exists — a dead
// link into an internal admin surface. The core origin is both addressable
// and the same value the 421 cross-jurisdiction redirect carries as
// `home_core_url`, so the two identically named fields finally agree.
//
// No longer gated on a host being configured: whether some URL map has an
// entry has nothing to do with whether this node hosts the account, and
// gating on it silently dropped the foreign_jurisdiction discriminator
// clients rely on to tell "hosted elsewhere" from "no profile yet".
if out.Body.Regional == nil && isForeign {
	out.Body.RegionalUnavailable = &corev1.MeRegionalUnavailable{
		Error:        "foreign_jurisdiction",
